# Gradle's build output and caches. Everything here is reproducible from the
# checked-in build files, and `app/build/` alone reaches tens of megabytes.
.gradle/
build/
app/build/
.kotlin/

# The SDK location, which is different on every machine. Checked in, it breaks
# everyone else's build; the README documents what it has to contain instead.
local.properties

# The release signing key's path, alias and passwords. The key itself lives outside
# the tree; this file is what points at it. Ignored because a signing key that
# reaches a repository has to be treated as compromised, and the password beside it
# makes that worse rather than better.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# The ad-hoc toolchain this project was developed against, if anyone mirrors the
# layout inside the tree.
jdk17/
gradle-8.9/
dl/

# Machine-local overrides, so a tracked file never carries one machine's paths.
# `tools\android-env.ps1` sources this when it exists; that is where this checkout's
# own SDK, JDK and local Gradle distribution are named.
tools/android-env.local.ps1

# Scratch from investigating a failure: a throwaway sshd config, a probe script,
# a captured transcript. The leading slash anchors them to the project root so a
# source directory could never be caught by accident.
/tmp-sshd/
/tmp-bridge/
*.out
*.err
# Development screenshots of the app in use, kept out of the repository on purpose:
# they show a real device book in the tab bar (label, host and user) and the phone's
# own status bar. They are evidence for the verification table in the README, not
# source, and they were moved beside the checkout. The directory is ignored rather
# than its contents, so a capture run that re-creates it stays untracked too.
.shots/